     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "The \u00a73Steam Engine\u00a7r is an early game method of turning \u00a7bSteam\u00a7r into energy. It requires an external source to provide steam and a way to dump or reprocess the \u00a7bLow-Pressure Steam\u00a7r it produces. \n\nThe Steam Engine has an energy efficiency of \u00a7e85%\u00a7r, making it better than the \u00a73Stirling Engine\u00a7r. However, it still has a throughput limit as it can only hold up to 2000 mB of steam. Its maximum processing rate is 2000 mB/t, producing a considerable \u00a7e3400 HE/t\u00a7r or \u00a7e68 kHE/s\u00a7r. It is therefore the best generator available before \u00a73Steam Turbines\u00a7r.\n\nA boiler being heated up by a heating oven using coal will produce \u00a7e17kHE/s\u00a7r.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
