     "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
     "completion_particle:8": "default",
     "isSilent:1": 0,
     "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
     "isMain:1": 0,
     "lockedProgress:1": 0,
     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "Fusion Reactor",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "The \u00a73Fusion Reactor\u00a7r is a large, expensive, and advanced reactor type that runs by fusing various plasma types to generate heat.\n\nThe main part of the fusion reactor, the \u00a73\"Torus\"\u00a7r, features four connecting ports for external components. It requires electricity and \u00a7bPerfluoromethyl\u00a7r cooling to operate.\n\nThe \u00a73Klystron\u00a7r is the main power source of the fusion reactor, which uses electricity and compressed air, to generate input energy, \u00a7eKyU\u00a7r, for the connected torus. It will throttle if the buffered electricity or compressed air falls below \u00a7e50%\u00a7r, and if it falls below the torus' required input level, the plasma will extinguish.\n\nThe different plasma types also generate different useful byproducts and differing levels of neutron flux for breeding bulk quantities of materials, such as \u00a76Lithium\u00a7r into \u00a76Tritium\u00a7r.\n\nWelding the coils will require a \u00a76Blowtorch\u00a7r or an \u00a76Acetylene Welding Torch\u00a7r.\n\nMore information can be found below:\n\n[url]https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/Fusion_Reactor[/url]\n\n\u00a72For the additional components and power generation methods, please check out the two quests below.\u00a7r\n\n\u00a72Multiple fusion reactors will be required soon so it is recommended that Bedrock Ore Processing and Oil Refinement is automated.\u00a7r",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
