     },
     "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
     "completion_particle:8": "default",
     "isSilent:1": 0,
     "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
     "isMain:1": 0,
     "lockedProgress:1": 0,
     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "Chicago Pile",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "The \u00a73Chicago Pile\u00a7r is a crude early-game breeding reactor meant to produce \u00a76Plutonium\u00a7r for use as reactor fuel.\n\nA pile is composed of drilled \u00a76Graphite\u00a7r which can hold a variety of items in it, including radioisotope rods (\u00a76Uranium\u00a7r, \u00a76Radium\u00a7r, \u00a76Plutonium\u00a7r), \u00a76Lithium rods\u00a7r, and control rods. It does not behave as a unified single block, instead each individual piece of drilled graphite interacts with each other piece in a unique way depending on the rod it contains.\n\nAfter sufficient flux, the uranium rods in the Chicago Pile will transmute into plutonium rods that can be processed in an anvil into \u00a76Reactor Grade Plutonium\u00a7r which can be used in other reactors such as the \u00a73ZIRNOX\u00a7r and \u00a73RBMK\u00a7r.\n\nThe chicago pile requires a significant amount of graphite blocks, which once placed can be drilled into with the hand drill to place any rod into. \n\nThe \u00a76Hand Drill\u00a7r can be used to drill holes into the graphite or take core samples of the uranium fuel to determine heat, depletion, and neutron flux. \u00a76Screwdrivers\u00a7r are used to extract rods.\n\nThe Quest asks for a 3x3 Chicago Pile (without the corners) with a \u00a76Ra226Be\u00a7r Rod in the center surrounded by Uranium Rods.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
