     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "Better Furnaces",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "OR",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "The \u00a73Bricked Furnace\u00a7r is almost the same as the vanilla furnace, but it can smelt construction materials faster, such as \u00a76Sand\u00a7r and \u00a76Cobblestone\u00a7r being smelted at double the speed. \u00a76Clay\u00a7r and \u00a76Fire Clay\u00a7r can be smelted at \u00a7e\u00a7rquadruple\u00a7r the speed, which means that making a full brick block can be done within a vanilla furnace operation. It can also make \u00a76Charcoal\u00a7r at double the speed. It can also collect Ashes from burnt fuel.\n\nThe \u00a73Iron Furnace\u00a7r has the base smelting speed \u00a7e20%\u00a7r faster than the vanilla furnace, which means it can complete an operation within 8 seconds instead of 10 seconds. Besides being able to smelt faster, it consumes fuel only during operation, so the fuel is never wasted. It also has burn time bonuses for various kinds of fuel, ranging from \u00a7e+25%\u00a7r for lignite to \u00a7e+100%\u00a7r for solid fuel.\n\n\u00a7dEt Futurum Requiem\u00a7r also backports modern furnaces, such as the \u00a73Smoker\u00a7r, which cooks food faster, and the \u00a73Blast Furnace\u00a7r, which smelts ores faster.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
