     "desc:8": "Oil products can be combusted or burnt to produce massive amounts of energy.\n\nThe \u00a73Industrial Combustion Engine\u00a7r combusts fuels, such as \u00a7bHeating Oil\u00a7r or \u00a7bDiesel\u00a7r to produce power. Various piston sets exist, which are needed for the engine to work, each one giving its own efficiency bonuses to fuel grades.\n\nThe \u00a74\u00a73Turbofan\u00a7r is the best place to use aviation type fuels, such as \u00a7bKerosene\u00a7r, as it provides \u00a7e100%\u00a7r power efficiency. Be careful not to stand infront of it while its operational!\n\nThe \u00a73Combined Cycle Gas Turbine\u00a7r is the only generator that can burn gaseous fuels at \u00a7e100%\u00a7r efficiency. The CCGT uses \u00a73\u00a7bEngine Lubricant\u00a7r, and produces \u00a7bDense Steam\u00a7r.\n\nThe \u00a73Flare Stack\u00a7r is used for burning gasses such as \u00a7bUnsaturated Hydrocarbons\u00a7r for power, aswell as dealing with excess fluids.\n\nThe \u00a73Fluid Burner\u00a7r is a much more efficient way of producing power from gases. Place a \u00a73Boiler\u00a7r ontop and run the \u00a7bSteam\u00a7r through a turbine to generate power.\n\nConsider installing a \u00a76Muffler\u00a7r on some of these machines as they are very loud. Shift-Click on a machine while holding a Muffler to apply.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
