     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "The \u00a73Stirling Engine\u00a7r uses heat from a \u00a73Heating Oven\u00a7r or a \u00a73\u00a7r\u00a73Firebox\u00a7r to produce power. If a Heating Oven is used to heat a Stirling engine, it will likely over-speed and damage it, sending the main gear flying. The heavy Stirling engine does not have this issue. \n\nA firebox running on coal with a stirling engine produces \u00a7e2kHE/s\u00a7r, while a heating oven with a heavy stirling engine produces \u00a7e10kHE/s\u00a7r.",
