  "253:10": {
   "tasks:9": {},
   "properties:10": {
    "betterquesting:10": {
     "visibility:8": "NORMAL",
     "icon:10": {
      "id:8": "appliedenergistics2:encoded_pattern",
      "Count:3": 1,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     },
     "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
     "completion_particle:8": "default",
     "isSilent:1": 0,
     "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
     "isMain:1": 0,
     "lockedProgress:1": 0,
     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "AE2 Autocrafting",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "\u00a72This quest serves an a guide on how to order items using the ME system. The example item will be an Analog Circuit.\u00a7r\n\nWith an \u00a73ME Drive\u00a7r providing item storage, a \u00a73Crafting CPU\u00a7r and \u00a73Interfaces\u00a7r, one can request any item to be crafted. The image below makes use of a \u00a73Molecular Assembler\u00a7r, a \u00a73Soldering Station\u00a7r, an \u00a73Electric Press\u00a7r aswell as two \u00a73Import Buses\u00a7r which serve as an output for the solderer and press.\n\n\n\nThe first step in automating crafting recipes is to encode \u00a76ME Patterns\u00a7r. There are two types of patterns, crafting and processing. The crafting pattern is created by having the \u00a73Pattern Terminal\u00a7r set to the crafting table. After placing the items in the terminal, press the arrow to finish encoding the recipe.\n\n\n\nFor recipes which arent made in a crafting table, such as the \u00a76Wires\u00a7r and the \u00a76Analog Circuit\u00a7r itself, the pattern terminal needs to be switched to the processing mode, which has a furnace icon.\n\n\n\nAfter all the patterns have been created, insert them into their respective interfaces.\nMake sure to enable blocking mode on the interfaces as not to have multiple different recipes enter the interface at once.\n\n\n\nFinally, after everything has been set up, the option to order items will be shown in the ME terminal.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
