  "272:10": {
   "tasks:9": {},
   "properties:10": {
    "betterquesting:10": {
     "visibility:8": "NORMAL",
     "icon:10": {
      "id:8": "appliedenergistics2:multi_part",
      "Count:3": 1,
      "Damage:2": 220,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     },
     "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
     "completion_particle:8": "default",
     "isSilent:1": 0,
     "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
     "isMain:1": 0,
     "lockedProgress:1": 0,
     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "ME Subnetting",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "\u00a7eSubnetworks\u00a7r are ME networks which can be accessed from a \u00a7eMain Network\u00a7r. In \u00a7dNTM\u00a7r\u00a7r they can be useful for storing items from passive processes without flooding the main storage network.\n\n\u00a72This quest serves as a guide on how to set up a subnet, which can be used to store the resourses that Bedrock Ore Processing produces.\u00a7r\n\nIn the image below are two ME networks, the \u00a7cRed\u00a7r one as the \u00a7cMainnet\u00a7r, and the \u00a79Blue\u00a7r one as the \u00a79Subnet\u00a7r.\n\n\n\nFor the purposes of this quest, the main network will store dirt blocks, while the subnet will store copper blocks.\n\n\n\n\n\nTo make the contents of the subnet, the copper blocks, visible to the main net, one must make an \u00a73Interface\u00a7r-\u00a73Storage Bus\u00a7r\u00a7r combo. The storage bus must be on the side of the main network.\n\n\n\nMake sure to filter the main network storage bus, and to also make it \"Extract Only\".\n\n\n\nNow the main network has access to materials stored on the sub network, which can be used for crafting.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
