  "277:10": {
   "tasks:9": {
    "0:10": {
     "index:3": 0,
     "groupDetect:1": 0,
     "requiredItems:9": {
      "0:10": {
       "Damage:2": 460,
       "Count:3": 2,
       "id:8": "appliedenergistics2:multi_part",
       "OreDict:8": ""
      }
     },
     "partialMatch:1": 1,
     "consume:1": 0,
     "autoConsume:1": 0,
     "taskID:8": "bq_standard:retrieval",
     "ignoreNBT:1": 1
    },
    "1:10": {
     "index:3": 1,
     "groupDetect:1": 0,
     "requiredItems:9": {
      "0:10": {
       "Damage:2": 0,
       "Count:3": 1,
       "id:8": "appliedenergistics2:memory_card",
       "OreDict:8": ""
      }
     },
     "partialMatch:1": 1,
     "consume:1": 0,
     "autoConsume:1": 0,
     "taskID:8": "bq_standard:retrieval",
     "ignoreNBT:1": 1
    }
   },
   "properties:10": {
    "betterquesting:10": {
     "visibility:8": "NORMAL",
     "icon:10": {
      "id:8": "appliedenergistics2:multi_part",
      "Count:3": 1,
      "Damage:2": 460,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     },
     "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
     "completion_particle:8": "default",
     "isSilent:1": 0,
     "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
     "isMain:1": 0,
     "lockedProgress:1": 0,
     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "P2P",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "\u00a76P2P\u00a7r Tunnel or \"Point to Point Tunnels\" are a versatile configurable system to move items / redstone / power / and fluids from one location to another though an existing ME Network without storage.\n\nTunnels are \u00a7e1 input to N outputs\u00a7r. This means you can output to as many points as you want, but only input at a single point per tunnel.\n\nNetworks can support any number of tunnels, of any different types, and they all function independently.\n\nME tunnels can be used to carry channels from one location to another, and can carry up to \u00a7e32 channels\u00a7r, same as a \u00a76ME Dense Cable\u00a7r, while only requiring a single channel per point, making tunnels a very powerful tool to expand me networks, especially over a distance. However with the great flex-ability they give you comes a limitation, the channel of a p2p tunnel cannot be carried by another p2p tunnel, meaning that you cannot nest them recursively.\n\nTo configure a P2P tunnel you must first attune the tunnel to carry what you want it to, then you need to configure the outputs to their input. You configure the connections by using the \u00a76Memory Card\u00a7r. First Shift+Right Click the input to save it on your memory card, then simply right click the different outputs to store the input onto the outputs. this also sets the type of the output to match the type of the input.\n\n\u00a72An advanced version of the Memory Card can also be made, which interacts with the entire network.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
   "rewards:9": {},
   "questID:3": 327,
   "preRequisites:11": [
    316
   ]
  },
  "278:10": {
   "tasks:9": {},
   "properties:10": {
    "betterquesting:10": {
     "visibility:8": "NORMAL",
     "icon:10": {
      "id:8": "appliedenergistics2:multi_part",
      "Count:3": 1,
      "Damage:2": 460,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     },
     "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
     "completion_particle:8": "default",
     "isSilent:1": 0,
     "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
     "isMain:1": 0,
     "lockedProgress:1": 0,
     "repeat_relative:1": 1,
     "questLogic:8": "AND",
     "name:8": "P2P ME Networking",
     "repeatTime:3": -1,
     "particle_count:3": -1,
     "countAsQuest:1": 1,
     "simultaneous:1": 0,
     "taskLogic:8": "AND",
     "autoClaim:1": 0,
     "globalShare:1": 0,
     "desc:8": "\u00a73P2P ME\u00a7r can be used to transport massive amounts of channels without laying many cables.\n\n\u00a72This quest serves as a guide on how to effectively use P2P ME.\u00a7r\n\nOnce an \u00a73Energy Acceptor\u00a7r has been set up, it is highly recommended (and likely needed) that an \u00a73Energy Cell\u00a7r is placed next to it as to ensure that there is enough power going to the system, as more components increase the energy demands of the ME system.\n\nAfter that, 2 \u00a73ME Controllers\u00a7r are required, one to provide the channels that machines will use, and another to transport the other's channels by the P2P connections. The top controller can be made bigger by attaching more controllers next to it.\n\n\n\nAfter the controllers are placed, on the top controller, a P2P Tunnel - ME needs to be placed on any side. The \u00a79Blue Cable\u00a7r will serve as the cable that connects the P2P connections, and as such, it needs to be connected to the bottom controller.\n\n\n\nBy linking the P2P connections together using a \u00a76Memory Card\u00a7r, the 32 channels from one side of the top controller will only use 1 channel from the bottom controller to be transported to any destination. The \u00a7cRed Cable\u00a7r now has access to 32 channels.\n\n\n\n\n\nBy expanding on the previous example, more connections can be added to fully utilize all channels.",
     "completion_animation:8": "default",
     "confetti_icon:10": {
      "id:8": "minecraft:stick",
      "Count:3": 0,
      "Damage:2": 0,
      "OreDict:8": ""
     }
    }
   },
   "rewards:9": {},
   "questID:3": 328,
   "preRequisites:11": [
    327
   ]
  },
